# Code owners for rossoctl/examples.
#
# Owners here are DERIVED from the project's source of truth for maintainership:
#   https://github.com/rossoctl/rossoctl/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md
#
# CODEOWNERS cannot reference that file, or any file: GitHub accepts only user and team
# handles, and it is read only from this repository's root, .github/ or docs/ -- there is no
# inheritance from rossoctl/rossoctl to lean on. So these names are a copy, and they have to
# be updated when MAINTAINERS.md changes.
#
# A rule naming a user or team that does not exist, or that lacks write access here, is
# silently ignored -- the matched paths end up with no owner and no warning. If you edit this
# file, confirm every handle still has access.

# Default owners for everything
* @rossoctl/maintainers

# CI and platform tooling. Gloire owns org-wide CI and repo governance; Ed owns the
# rossoctl-cli and has written most of the Makefile.
.github/ @rubambiza
Makefile @esnible

# A2A agents and MCP tools
a2a/ @pdettori
mcp/ @pdettori

# Documentation. There is no docs/ directory in this repo -- the previous rule for it
# matched nothing. Each example documents itself in its own README.
*.md @rossoctl/maintainers
